WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.089
Good morning Hank it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.089 --> 00:00:05.380
So you may remember back in the halcyon days
of 2007 when I was young and clean-shaven

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.600
and the state of Illinois had a budget, our
YouTube channel had a resident mathematician,

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:11.600
Daniel Biss.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.680
So Daniel and I became friends in 2003 just
after he got his PhD from MIT; that's a lot

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.580
of letters for a numbers guy.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.650
I'm sorry, I want to apologize to my friends,
my family.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.910
I am deeply ashamed of that joke.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:26.150
But anyway, when I met Daniel, he was a math
professor at the University of Chicago, only

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:29.630
he didn't have to teach any classes and he
also wasn't required to publish, he just sort

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:31.560
of had to think about math.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.950
Daniel was a good person with a good life.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.300
So, Hank, you can imagine my surprise when
Daniel told me one day that he no longer wanted

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.030
to be a mathematician with a tenure track
professorship at the University of Chicago

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:44.489
and instead wanted to be a member of the Illinois
State House of Representatives.

00:00:44.489 --> 00:00:49.079
I mean, Daniel is charming and funny and intelligent,
but he did not strike me as a politician,

00:00:49.079 --> 00:00:51.020
least of all an Illinois politician.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.829
One ought not generalize about a class of
individuals, of course, Hank, but between

00:00:53.829 --> 00:00:59.879
1961 and 2013, most of the people who served
as Governor of Illinois were later imprisoned

00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:00.879
for corruption.

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:03.460
Not a couple, not some, most.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.590
But Daniel seemed to genuinely believe that
government service was noble and important,

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:12.609
so back in 2008, Nerdfighteria helped raise
money for his campaign, and he lost, but then

00:01:12.609 --> 00:01:16.649
in 2010, he won, and then in 2012, he was
elected to the Illinois State Senate.

00:01:16.649 --> 00:01:18.590
Daniel is a Democrat, but he's widely respected.

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:22.119
In fact, I once met a Republican member of
the Illinois House who told me Daniel Biss

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:25.409
is one of the smartest people I have ever
met, only he didn't say people, he said a

00:01:25.409 --> 00:01:26.409
curse word.

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:29.369
Daniel is also one of the smartest curse words
I've ever met, and he turns out to be a really

00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:30.759
effective politician.

00:01:30.759 --> 00:01:34.169
He passed a hugely important retirement savings
bill in Illinois, he passed a law banning

00:01:34.169 --> 00:01:37.060
so-called "conversion therapy" for LGBT youth.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.880
He's also been a big advocate for privacy,
especially when it comes to technology, like

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:43.719
he passed a bill saying that police can't
use surveillance drones without a search warrant,

00:01:43.719 --> 00:01:47.439
and I have to say, he's kind of made me believe
in politics again, like, in an age of American

00:01:47.439 --> 00:01:51.770
ideologues, he's this practical and sensible
person who genuinely wants to make people's

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:52.880
lives suck less.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.700
And refreshingly, he doesn't use inflammatory
rhetoric.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:59.009
Meanwhile, the state of Illinois is careening
toward disaster.

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:01.700
See, I know how to use inflammatory rhetoric.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:05.719
Illinois has over 100 billion dollars in pension
debt, which is unique in the country.

00:02:05.719 --> 00:02:09.530
It also has a poor credit rating, and it's
currently operating without a budget, which

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:13.879
has led to, if I may quote Daniel, "An insane
patchwork quilt of incomprehensible nonsense."

00:02:13.879 --> 00:02:15.890
That's not inflammatory, that's factual.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:20.030
Like, one example of this incomprehensible
nonsense, the Illinois State Museum has closed

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:24.560
because of budget cuts, but all of its employees
are still going to work and getting paid.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.799
Neither the Republican governor nor the Democratic
leaders of the state legislature are at all

00:02:28.799 --> 00:02:33.500
serious about the kinds of reform that are
needed to end Illinois' decades of fiscal

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.500
mismanagement.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.500
If I were Daniel, I would find all of that
so annoying.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.500
Daniel: When I find something immensely frustrating,
I ask myself, "Am I frustrated because something

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.500
is broken and corrupt, or am I frustrated
because I don't get to be the Emperor?

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.500
And every time it's option B, I remind myself
that's actually a positive thing, because

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:44.730
this way we never have a Mussolini.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:52.420
People of goodwill need to be willing to accept
that slowness.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:59.250
Otherwise, the process gets taken over by
people who are deliberately trying to steal

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.250
from it."

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:01.250
John: Alright, so Daniel is now running for
comptroller of Illinois.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.050
If you don't know what a comptroller is, don't
worry, I didn't know either, until Daniel

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.050
told me.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.079
It's basically like the chief financial officer
for the state.

00:03:07.079 --> 00:03:10.829
And I want Daniel to win, not because he's
my friend, but because he's a smart and independent

00:03:10.829 --> 00:03:14.890
voice, and he's also very good at math, which
is a useful skill for a comptroller.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:19.519
But here's the thing, politics, in some ways,
especially local politics, are run by money.

00:03:19.519 --> 00:03:23.890
Running for comptroller, a job I'd never heard
of until my friend ran for it, costs millions

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:24.890
of dollars.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:28.999
So if you wanna know what's wrong with American
politics, just remember that campaigns for

00:03:28.999 --> 00:03:32.620
Illinois State Comptroller cost millions of
dollars.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:34.719
So I'm going to do a fundraiser for Daniel
next month.

00:03:34.719 --> 00:03:37.159
In fact, it'll be my last public appearance
before VidCon.

00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:39.939
The tickets are $40, which I know is a lot,
I'm sorry, but everybody who goes will get

00:03:39.939 --> 00:03:42.659
a copy of An Abundance of Katherines, signed
by both Daniel and me.

00:03:42.659 --> 00:03:43.769
I hope to see some of you there.

00:03:43.769 --> 00:03:47.420
You can also donate to Daniel's campaign directly
at danielbiss.com, and regardless of your

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:50.870
political beliefs, if you're lucky enough
to live in a country where your voice matters,

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:53.189
I would encourage you to get involved in the
political process.

00:03:53.189 --> 00:03:56.810
One thing I've learned from Daniel is that
good, honest people in politics really can

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:57.810
make a difference.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:58.739
Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

